    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\overrightarrow{AP}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{BP}=0$, so $\\angle APB=90^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{AP}&=(r\\cos\\theta-(-r),r\\sin\\theta)\\\\&=(r\\cos\\theta+r,r\\sin\\theta)\\\\\\overrightarrow{BP}&=(r\\cos\\theta-r,r\\sin\\theta)\\\\\\overrightarrow{AP}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{BP}&=(r\\cos\\theta+r)(r\\cos\\theta-r)+r^2\\sin^2\\theta\\\\&=r^2\\cos^2\\theta-r^2+r^2\\sin^2\\theta\\\\&=r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)-r^2\\\\&=r^2-r^2\\\\&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince P is neither A nor B, both vectors are nonzero and hence perpendicular. Reversing both gives $\\overrightarrow{PA}\\perp\\overrightarrow{PB}$, so $\\angle APB=90^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
